      <CalendarUID>-1</CalendarUID><FreeformDurationFormat>7</FreeformDurationFormat><EffortDriven>1</EffortDriven>
      <Notes>Maintenance window execution sequence: (1) Disable all BizTalk receive locations and stop all host instances. (2) Take final tail-log backups of all BizTalk databases on source SQL. (3) Launch parallel restore sessions — DBA-A restores SQL-A databases, DBA-B restores SQL-B databases simultaneously. (4) WAIT for both restore streams to complete WITH RECOVERY before proceeding. (5) Apply logins to SQL-A and SQL-B. Migrate SQL Agent jobs to owning server. (6) Update SampleUpdateInfo.xml with both SQL-A and SQL-B server names. Run UpdateDatabase.vbs. (7) Start BizTalk host instances and re-enable receive locations. (8) Validate message flow on each integration endpoint.</Notes>
      <Hyperlink>How to Move the BizTalk Server Databases</Hyperlink>
      <HyperlinkAddress>https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/biztalk/core/how-to-move-the-biztalk-server-databases</HyperlinkAddress>
    </Task>
